+\code{dv_spec(prey_name = )}.}
+
+\item{placeholders}{Lower-case values treated as "not identified".}
+}
+\value{
+\code{data} with one column per rank (and \code{name_col}).
+}
+\description{
+Metabarcoding pipelines (QIIME 2, DADA2, mothur, SILVA, Greengenes, MIDORI,
+BOLD, a BLAST against GenBank) report each sequence's taxonomy as one
+string, such as \code{"k__Animalia; p__Arthropoda; c__Copepoda; g__Calanus; s__finmarchicus"}. \code{dv_parse_lineage()} splits that string into one column
+per rank, so the data can be prepared with \code{dv_prepare(taxonomy = "columns")}, keeping the reference taxonomy the sequences were assigned
+with (NCBI, SILVA, BOLD ...), or only the deepest name can be passed on to
+WoRMS or GBIF.
+}
+\details{
+Two layouts are read:
+\itemize{
+\item \strong{prefixed} - each field starts with a rank code (\code{k__}, \code{d__},
+\code{p__}, \code{c__}, \code{o__}, \code{f__}, \code{g__}, \code{s__}; also \verb{k:}/\verb{p:} and
+\verb{kingdom:}); fields are placed by their code, so missing ranks are
+allowed. \code{d__} (domain) is ignored unless \code{"domain"} is a rank;
+\item \strong{positional} - plain names in rank order (\code{"Animalia;Arthropoda; ..."}); the i-th field goes to the i-th rank of \code{ranks}.
+}
