+positional strings, give \code{ranks} in the order of the fields: MIDORI and
+NCBI lineages start with a superkingdom, not a kingdom, so use e.g.
+\code{ranks = c("domain", "phylum", "class", "order", "family", "genus", "species")} and the same \code{ranks} in \code{\link[=dv_spec]{dv_spec()}}.
+Placeholders such as an empty field, \code{"NA"}, \code{"unassigned"},
+\code{"unclassified"}, \code{"uncultured"}, \code{"unidentified"}, \code{"unknown"},
+\code{"metagenome"} or a species written \code{"Genus sp."} become \code{NA}, so the
+record is shown as unidentified at that rank. Trailing NCBI tax IDs
